  "body": " Square Root Property   Solving Equations using Square Root Property   Square Root Theorem   Let . If , then .     Using Factoring and the Square Root Property to Solve an Equation   Solve .            Note that the GCF is . We can factor it out and then use the Zero Product Property along with the Square Root Property to solve for .     Therefore, the solutions are and .     Factoring vs. Square Root Property  We could have factored as a difference of squares to get . We end up at the same solutions, but the square root property is a more intuitive path for completing this problem than difference of squares.    Do Not Divide by x  When one side of the equation equals , do not divide by after factoring it out. Dividing by removes the equation from consideration, leaving only . As a result, you would miss the solution , which is part of the complete solution set.     Solving Equations Involving Perfect Square Trinomials  While the -method works for any trinomial, certain forms do not require the -method. They are called perfect square trinomials .   Perfect Square Trinomials   Let and be any real, nonzero numbers. Then the following two equations are true.        How to Recognize Perfect Square Trinomials   If you notice that the coefficient of and the constant term are both perfect squares, it is worth checking if you have a perfect square trinomial. In order to do this:    Take the square root of the coefficient of and the constant term.  Multiply these resulting numbers together.  See if the coefficient of is twice those numbers. If it is, you can use one of the above equations.   The equation you use is based on the sign of the coefficient of .  If the coefficient of is positive, use the identity .  If the coefficient of is negative, use the identity .          How To Factor Perfect Square Trinomials   Consider . Since  and   and is 2 times 8,  we can use the equation with and . Therefore, we have      Solving a Perfect Square Trinomial Using the Square Root Property   Solve the equation .         Since and , we have and . Their product , and notice that is times . Therefore, is a perfect square trinomial. We can factor it and use the factorization to solve for .     Therefore, our only solution is .     Solving a Perfect Square Trinomial Using the Square Root Property   Solve the equation .         Since and , we have and . Their product , and notice that is times . Therefore, is a perfect square trinomial. We can factor it and use the factorization to solve for .     Therefore, our only solution is .     "
