  "title": "Modeling Simple Harmonic Motion.",
  "body": " Modeling Simple Harmonic Motion   An object that moves on the coordinate-plane is in simple harmonic motion if its distance from its equilibrium position at time can be modeled by a function of the form or , where   the amplitude measures the maximum displacement of the object from its equilibrium position, and    the period measures the time it takes for the object to complete one full cycle of motion.      "
