  "title": "Representations of the Same Polar Point.",
  "body": " Representations of the Same Polar Point   Let be any polar coordinate. Points of the following forms represent the same point in the plane.   Any point of the form , where is any integer.  What this says that as long as you are on the same circle of radius , all angles coterminal to will represent the same point.      Any point of the form , where is any integer.  What this says is that if you flip the sign of , all angles coterminal to will represent the same point.        "
